WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.400
SPEAKER: Hello.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.420
Welcome to the session on
building the right API team.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.232
As part of this
video, we'll talk you

00:00:11.232 --> 00:00:12.690
through our
recommendations when it

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.050
comes to forming your API
team, the responsibilities,

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.350
and the various roles involved.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.630
So to start things
off, let's take a look

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.590
at the digital value chain.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.540
You might have seen
this diagram before.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.170
But to briefly explain,
the digital value chain

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.510
shows the relationship
between the various teams

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.090
and technologies from
the end consumer,

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.220
all the way down to
the back end systems.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.040
For this session, we'll
be focusing specifically

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.440
on the API team, shown
here in the chain.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.910
The API team builds--

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.180
yep, you guessed it-- the APIs.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.760
This is the team that will be
working directly with your API

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.110
platform to create lovable
APIs for your app developers.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:57.040
In terms of responsibility, the
API team owns five core areas.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.020
First is building
highly consumable APIs.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.270
The key word here is consumable.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.240
We recommend approaching API
design and implementation

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.840
from the outside in,
rather than the inside out.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.450
What this means is that
the API team will always

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.650
need to keep the end consumer
in mind when approaching APIs.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.000
In the case of our
digital value chain,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.280
this is the app developer.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.680
The API team should
always be asking itself,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.260
if I were an app developer,
what type of APIs

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.030
would I want to consume?

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.810
Second is learning and applying
best practices to the APIs

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.280
that they will be building.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.710
We promote a variety of
industry best practices

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.800
when it comes to the design,
development, and the deployment

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.660
of your APIs.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.840
Please refer to the docs page
or a self-service training

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.240
on Coursera for
additional details.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.520
Third is engagement.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.520
Similar to our focus
on consumable APIs,

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.340
the API team should be
engaged with all the players

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.720
in the digital value chain.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.900
This includes back
end system teams,

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.870
which the APIs will front
to the app developer

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.000
in order to gain valuable
insights to unearth areas

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.220
to further iterate on and to
enhance your existing services.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.080
Scalability is
also very important

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.860
when it comes to
your API program.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.700
Oftentimes, we see that the API
team starts small, but grows

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.430
rapidly as more and more
demand comes down the pipeline.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:25.060
In these scenarios, federation
becomes very important.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.760
The API team owns the
creation and the management

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.400
of materials that allows
for the entire organization

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.110
to rapidly scale.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:35.410
This includes things like the
API Playbook, automated test

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.160
suites, and more.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.360
Finally, API should
always be improving.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.340
By leveraging capabilities
of the platform,

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.060
such as analytics, the API team
can gain valuable insight into

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.370
who's using the APIs and how.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.500
This information
allows the API team

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.490
to find areas of improvement and
enhancements based on real data

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:55.780
that they are seeing.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.000
Remember our focus
on consumer ability?

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.730
This information can
help a lot with that.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.040
We strongly believe in the
fast and iterative approach

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.510
to development.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.300
Market shifts happen
rapidly, and your API team

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.270
needs to be able to adapt and
be flexible in its delivery

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.760
approach.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.040
As a result, we
recommend a methodology

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.620
such as Agile for your program.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.100
Similarly, the API team is
composed in a similar fashion

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.610
to a standard scrum team.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.400
A diverse set of perspectives
is also very important,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.850
which we'll cover in more
detail when we talk about roles.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.490
Having different viewpoints
that encompass the business,

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.850
technical, and operational
views will streamline your API

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.510
development process.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.130
So now that we've
covered the basics,

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.450
let's jump into the individual
roles of an API team.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.630
There are five main roles when
it comes to a good API team.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:47.810
They are the API team
leader, the architect,

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.390
the API developers,
the evangelists,

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.250
and the extended team.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.920
Let's spend the next few
minutes going over each one.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.770
The API team leader is
essentially a product owner.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.610
Now, note that I said product
owner and not project manager.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.520
As mentioned before, the
API team we're suggesting

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.690
is based off the
standard scrum model.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.570
So the API team
leader is essentially

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:11.210
your product owner in scrum.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.280
As such, the team
leader should be

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.710
aligned with both the
business and the city

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:18.769
and have a good understanding of
the needs of the end consumer,

00:04:18.769 --> 00:04:21.110
for example, the app developer.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:25.160
The team leader also helps
create, refine, and prioritize

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.700
the scope for the API team.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.650
When it comes down to
it, the team leader

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:32.630
will be the one that makes the
call if trade-offs are needed

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.320
in the event that the API team
doesn't have the bandwidth

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.300
to complete all the items.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.340
The architect is
critical to the API team.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.880
Not only do they bridge the
gap between the API team

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.370
leader and the API
developers, they also

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.160
establish and enforce
API best practices

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.130
and keep a common
design cadence.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:54.490
Their approach to the API
design is consumer-focused

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:57.460
and educates the
wider API team on how

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.680
to leverage the API platform.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.680
In summary, they're part
designer, part teacher,

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.680
and part enforcer.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.342
The API developers is your
core development group.

00:05:07.342 --> 00:05:09.300
At the end of the day,
these are the folks that

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.780
are going to get the job done.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:13.200
The API developers will
look to the API team

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.320
leader for guidance on the
scope and the architect

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.450
for their design principles.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:22.680
They will then take those inputs
and build out the actual APIs.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.960
As you would expect,
the API developers

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.200
should be very familiar
with the API platform.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.990
Without the API developers,
nothing will get built.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:33.300
So be sure you're nice to them.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.750
The evangelist is the
mascot for the API program.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.570
They are responsible for not
only outreaching to your API

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.000
consumers, but also
creating and nurturing

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.090
a developer community.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.740
They can provide
valuable feedback

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.540
from the field, which
can then directly

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.780
impact the direction
of the API program.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.210
A good evangelist will
be critical in expanding

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.700
the audience of your
APIs, both within

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.740
and outside of
your organization.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:01.070
The extended team is also very
important in getting your APIs

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.680
out to production.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.480
The extended team
covers organizations,

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.710
such as security, QA,
operations, and others.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.990
The extended team
and their processes

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.870
may vary depending on how
your organization is set up,

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.790
but the key takeaway
is that these teams

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:19.130
should support, rather than
obstruct, your time to market.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:22.120
So before we wrap up, let's
cover some common attributes

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.960
that all successful
API teams have.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.470
First, a successful API
team should have the support

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.970
of an executive sponsor.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:33.190
Chances are, the API
team will continue

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.990
to push the envelope
of innovation

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.740
within your organization.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:38.890
So having a strong
executive sponsor

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.050
can help clear any
of these roadblocks

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.580
that they may face when
challenging the status quo.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:48.930
Second, the API team should
be solely focused on APIs.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:52.500
We often see API teams consist
of developers who are also

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.830
shared with other projects.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.870
This not only can lead to issues
with resourcing and bandwidth,

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:00.230
but also affect the
direction of your APIs,

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.360
such as cutting corners
and striving away

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.770
from best practices.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.380
Third, there must be a
willingness to train others

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.150
within the organization.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.420
As your API program
grows, so will the demand.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:14.480
This, in turn, can lead to
an influx of APIs that will

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.510
need to be created or enhanced.

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:21.120
Chances are, the API team that
you start off with will expand.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.730
And as new members
are brought in,

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.980
they'll need to be trained
on the foundational design

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.960
philosophies you've
already established.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.050
In the world of APIs and the
consumer-focused approach,

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.240
a consistent API
experience is key.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.200
Fourth, the API team should have
a direct line to the business.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.390
There shouldn't be any
silos between the business

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:40.960
and technical teams.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.480
Makes sense, right?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.060
If the API team has a better
understanding of the business

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.760
vision and the impacts
to the end consumers,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.920
the better the APIs
will be, since they

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.380
will ensure that the business
vision is properly achieved.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.710
Finally, the API
team should be free

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.780
from pre-existing constraints.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:00.090
As we mentioned
before, the API team

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.220
should strive on
innovation, and not

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:06.480
be constrained by outdated
governance models or processes.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.640
In the world of
APIs, time to market

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.830
is critical, so
welcome change, rather

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:14.100
than trying to fit it within
an insufficient process.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.140
In closing, we
totally understand

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.850
if the concepts
discussed in this video

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.550
may seem a little challenging,
especially if you already

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:24.220
have a governance or delivery
structure in place today.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:27.060
Remember that the start always
requires the greatest effort.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.160
But if you can overcome
these challenges

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.140
and embrace the ideas
we just covered,

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:34.710
you'll have a more robust
and innovative API team.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.620
Thank you.

